",[75],[76,77],36.92653,14.74761,{"_":79,"type":80,"subtype":81,"geo":82,"geoCert":85},"Found in Contrada San Martino, on the left bank of the Irminio, near San Giacomo (c.5km north-west of Ragusa), close to a small group of artificial rock-cut tombs.","found","discovered",[83,84],36.9740823,14.7971441,"medium",[83,84],{"_":88,"type":89,"subtype":90,"geo":17},"None","observed","autopsied",[],"Sicily","",{"_":95,"mainLang":96,"languages":97},"Ancient Greek","grc",[95],{"type":99,"bibl":100},"edition",[101],{"author":102,"date":103,"citedRange":104,"ptr":105,"ref":107,"inscriptionDate":103,"title":109,"citation":110,"uri":111,"year":103},"Scerra","2018","470-471, figs. 4-5",{"target":106},"http://zotero.org/groups/382445/items/BKW9Q5A5",{"_":108,"target":108},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002691","Le necropoli di età greca dall'Irminio a Camarina : vecchi dati, recenti acquisizioni e nuove considerazioni su popolamento, commerci e culti","\u003Cspan>Saverio Scerra, «Le necropoli di età greca dall’Irminio a Camarina : vecchi dati, recenti acquisizioni e nuove considerazioni su popolamento, commerci e culti», in \u003Ci>Ollus leto datus est : architettura, topografia e rituali funerari nelle necropoli delli Italia meridionale e delle Sicilia tra antichità e medioevo : atti del convegno internazionale di studi Reggio Calabria, 22-25 ottobre 2013 1: Dalla preistoria all’ellenismo\u003C/i>, a c. di Carmela Malacrino e Simonetta Bonomi (Reggio di Calabria: Museo Archeologico Nazionale di Reggio Calabria, 2018), 465–74\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/BKW9Q5A5",{"type":113,"bibl":114},"discussion",[17],{"editor":116,"principal":119,"contributors":122,"change":133},{"_":117,"ref":118},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":120,"ref":121},"Valentina Mignosa","#VM",[123,126,130],{"_":117,"xml:id":124,"ref":125},"JP","http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":127,"xml:id":128,"ref":129},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":120,"xml:id":131,"ref":132},"VM","https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511",{"_":134,"when":135,"who":121},"Creation of file and EpiDoc encoding","2026-07-31",[],[138],"Scerra, 2018, Le necropoli di età greca dall'Irminio a Camarina : vecchi dati, recenti acquisizioni e nuove considerazioni su popolamento, commerci e culti",[140],"BKW9Q5A5",[142,143,144,19,23,27,145,146,147,148,96],"isic004498","epitaph of aischylos",{"_":5},"hybla heraea","ragusa","sicily","ancient greek",[],{"title":151,"body":152,"divs":153,"editions":178,"images":188,"handnote":189},"ISic004498. Epitaph of Aischylos","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\n                    ἐιμὶ τοῦ Γο\n                    ργου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\">Αἰσχύλου\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[ἐ?]ιμὶ τοῦ \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Γο\n                    ργου\">Γ[ο-]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ργου\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\n                    ἐιμὶ τοῦ Γο\n                    ργου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\">ΑΙΣΧΥΛΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[.]ΙΜΙΤΟΥ\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Γο\n                    ργου\">Γ[.]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ΡΓΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after photograph in Scerra 2018\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>I belong to Aischylos, [son] of Gorgos.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The inscription follows a funerary formula characteristic of Greek Sicily, consisting of the name of the deceased in the genitive, the first-person verb εἰμί and the patronymic. The three lines are separated by horizontal incised rules, an unusual feature in early lapidary inscriptions, as is the spelling -ου for the long close vowel /oː/, especially given the context. The letters tend towards vertical alignment. The semicircular gamma, rho with a descending appendage and cross-shaped chi support a date between the end of the sixth and the beginning of the fifth century BCE. The slab was found close to a group of artificial rock-cut tombs and probably served as the closing slab of one of them. Scerra interprets the inscription as evidence for the adoption of Greek language and funerary practices within the indigenous settlement of Contrada San Martino.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Scerra 2018 470-471, figs. 4-5 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002691\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002691\u003C/a>  \u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\"> Line 1-3    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[154,157,160,163,166,169,172,175],{"id":155,"html":156},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\n                    ἐιμὶ τοῦ Γο\n                    ργου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\">Αἰσχύλου\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[ἐ?]ιμὶ τοῦ \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Γο\n                    ργου\">Γ[ο-]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ργου\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Valentina Mignosa\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\n                    ἐιμὶ τοῦ Γο\n                    ργου\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Αἰσχύλου\">ΑΙΣΧΥΛΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>[.]ΙΜΙΤΟΥ\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Γο\n                    ργου\">Γ[.]\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>ΡΓΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>",{"id":158,"html":159},"facsimile-images","\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>",{"id":161,"html":162},"apparatus","\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text after photograph in Scerra 2018\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>",{"id":164,"html":165},"translation","\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>I belong to Aischylos, [son] of Gorgos.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":167,"html":168},"commentary","\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The inscription follows a funerary formula characteristic of Greek Sicily, consisting of the name of the deceased in the genitive, the first-person verb εἰμί and the patronymic. The three lines are separated by horizontal incised rules, an unusual feature in early lapidary inscriptions, as is the spelling -ου for the long close vowel /oː/, especially given the context. The letters tend towards vertical alignment. The semicircular gamma, rho with a descending appendage and cross-shaped chi support a date between the end of the sixth and the beginning of the fifth century BCE. The slab was found close to a group of artificial rock-cut tombs and probably served as the closing slab of one of them. Scerra interprets the inscription as evidence for the adoption of Greek language and funerary practices within the indigenous settlement of Contrada San Martino.\u003C/p>  ",{"id":170,"html":171},"bibliography","\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Scerra 2018 470-471, figs. 4-5 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002691\"